{
  "_schema_note": "date is the calendar date (America/New_York) this cache was computed for, YYYY-MM-DD. tickers.<TICKER> fields: rsi (T-1 daily RSI-14), ma20, ma_50d, ma_20d_prev (MA20 as of ma20_slope_lookback_days trading days ago, for slope check), atr20, pct_from_high, t1_close, t1_low_5d_min / t1_low_5d_min_prev (min close of the most recent 5 trading days and the 5 before that, for Higher Low confirmation), ma_5d, t1_volume, vol_20ma (20-day average volume, for volume-expansion confirmation), next_earnings_date (YYYY-MM-DD or null). Recomputed once per calendar date, first run of the day that sees a stale/missing date refreshes it. Same fields also apply to market-index tickers used for market_risk_mode (VIX/QQQ/SOXX) when relevant. swing_current_state / swing_trend_state / swing_last_high / swing_last_low / swing_reversal_threshold_used: output of lib/swing_structure.py's compute_swing_structure() (main branch git show main:lib/swing_structure.py, see docs/takeprofit-infq-spec-v3.1.md), computed from >=1 year of already-closed daily OHLC (today's still-forming bar always excluded -- this is the caller's responsibility per the module's own docstring). swing_current_state / swing_trend_state use the module's fixed enums (HH_CONFIRMED/HL_CONFIRMED/LH_CONFIRMED/LL_CONFIRMED/INSUFFICIENT_DATA, and BULLISH/BEARISH/TRANSITIONAL/UNKNOWN respectively). swing_last_high / swing_last_low are each either null or {date, price} for the most recently confirmed swing point of that kind -- these feed the take-profit routine's Trailing Stop event id and candidate formula. swing_previous_low is the same shape (or null) for the swing low confirmed immediately before swing_last_low -- display-only, used by the routine's structural Lower-Low risk alert to show \"old low -> new low\" in the Telegram message, never read by any decision logic. IMPORTANT: the date component inside swing_last_high/swing_last_low MUST be normalized to a plain \"YYYY-MM-DD\" string (no time-of-day, no timezone offset) before being written here -- never write through whatever raw string compute_swing_structure()'s date field happens to produce, since that depends on how the caller's own OHLC dataframe index was built and is not guaranteed to be byte-identical across different runs (each trigger regenerates its own script). The take-profit routine's lh_event_id is a straight equality string comparison against state.json's last_processed_lh_event, so any drift in this date string's format between the day an event was first cached and a later day silently breaks the ATR-freeze guarantee (looks like a 'new' event every time, so atr_at_event keeps recomputing instead of staying frozen). Recomputed once per calendar date alongside the other T-1 indicators above; a ticker with insufficient history (per the module's own INSUFFICIENT_DATA rule) caches that state as-is, never force-computed from padded data.",
